~ start
if Story.is_set("met_chant_trembling")
	=> after_chant
else
	# Before talking to Chauntecleer: Saberhagen only sings his jingle.
	# Type the jingle line in place of the placeholder below.
	Saberhagen: Meow meow meow meow, meow meow meow meow. (CAT JINGLE)
	=> END

~ after_chant
Saberhagen The Warlock: Meow.
- Tricks are for kids.
	=> riddle
- Leave.
	=> END
~ riddle
Saberhagen The Warlock: Dogs guard. Cats watch... and judge. (Saberhagen snickers)
- Dogs
	Saberhagen The Warlock: Minerva keeps me on a tight leash, but for how long?
	Saberhagen The Warlock: You should kill me, warrior, while you have the chance.
	=> riddle
- Cats
	Saberhagen The Warlock: Sometimes, warrior, I feel you have forgotten me. Here I wait until I am freed of my curse.
	Saberhagen The Warlock: Do not worry. I will not forget the kindness you have shown me.
	Saberhagen The Warlock: I also will not kill you. I will keep you as my pet.
	=> riddle
- Judge
	Saberhagen The Warlock: I sit on Minervas windowsill all day and judge every soul that passes.
	Saberhagen The Warlock: The tracker who is brave only when the sun is up. The wild one who pines for an old woman. The light that I will capture.
	Saberhagen The Warlock: How is your wife, Warrior?
	Saberhagen The Warlock: Still flickering in that box, waiting for a savior?
	Saberhagen The Warlock: I could help you. I raised her body once. Kept it... very well preserved. (He purrs.)
	Saberhagen The Warlock: I am sure she would...[wait=0.8] [shake rate=25 level=10][color=#E98B83]DIE FOR A BODY!![/color][/shake]
	=> END
- Leave.
	=> END
=> END
